Characteristics:
In a linear bonding curve, the price of a token increases steadily as the supply increases.
The slope (constant 
𝑏
b) determines how fast the price increases.
Early buyers don’t benefit as much from a price advantage, but the price remains more stable as supply grows.
Use Case: Linear bonding curves are often used when you want a predictable and steady price increase. It’s suitable for cases where both early and late buyers should have similar price access, though earlier participants still get a slight advantage.
2. Exponential Bonding Curve
Formula: 
