b are constants that shape the curve.
Characteristics:
In an exponential bonding curve, the token price increases rapidly as the supply grows.
Early buyers benefit significantly from much lower prices, while late buyers experience steep price increases as more tokens are minted.
Use Case: Exponential bonding curves are ideal when you want to incentivize early participation, as early buyers benefit from low prices. This type of curve is common in projects with speculative dynamics, where scarcity of tokens leads to a higher price for later participants.
3. Logarithmic Bonding Curve
