Characteristics:
Early tokens are very expensive.
The price decreases as more tokens are minted, making later tokens cheaper.
Use Case:
For projects that want to start with high-value tokens and reward long-term buyers with more affordable prices.
10. Flat Bonding Curve (Fixed Price)

In a flat bonding curve, the price of the token does not change with supply. All tokens are sold at a fixed price, no matter how many have been minted or bought.

Formula:
