Characteristics:
Price only increases when the supply reaches predefined thresholds.
More predictable than some other models, since price increments happen at precise points.
Use Case:
Token sales with multiple phases, where a certain number of tokens must be sold before moving to the next pricing tier.
14. Quadratic Bonding Curve

A quadratic bonding curve increases more steeply than a linear curve but less so than an exponential one. It’s often used when early buyers are favored, but price increases are more gradual than in exponential models.

