Use Case:
Quadratic curves can be used for projects that want a balance between incentivizing early buyers and maintaining long-term sustainability.
15. Hyperbolic Tangent Bonding Curve (tanh Curve)

A tanh (hyperbolic tangent) curve is similar to a sigmoid curve but with slightly different mathematical characteristics. It’s useful when you want early rapid price increases that then taper off.

